; An ordinary zone.  Nothing in it is wrong: what is wrong is the name
; in the signer field of every signature over it, which says a zone
; that did not sign them and whose key would not verify them.
;
; The parent carries a DS here, so a resolver has been told to check --
; which is the difference between this and jp.sharp, where the same
; signatures sit under a delegation with no DS and nobody looks.
$ORIGIN example.
$TTL 3600
@	IN	SOA	ns.example. root.example. 1 3600 900 604800 3600
@	IN	NS	ns.example.
ns	IN	{{AUTH_ADDR_RR}}
www	IN	A	192.0.2.1
